# INFOBASE Safety Guardrails

## Destructive Action Controls

- Never run destructive commands without explicit human confirmation.
- Forbidden without confirmation: broad delete operations, irreversible git resets, destructive DB updates.
- Prefer reversible edits and targeted changes.

## Secrets and Sensitive Data

- Never print or commit secrets from `.env` or platform secret stores.
- Never hardcode passwords, API keys, or tokens in code/docs.
- Use `.env.example` as the only env template.

## Quality Gates

- For substantive code changes, run `npm run lint`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build`.
- If checks fail due to pre-existing issues, report clearly and avoid masking failures.

## Documentation and Traceability

- Update docs when behavior, setup steps, or security posture changes.
- Include a concise risk note for known limitations or unresolved issues.

## Human Approval Required

- Any production-impacting operation
- Any access-control change
- Any data-destructive operation
